# Decorator placement

Prettier does **not** rewrite decorator layout. Always generate class property decorators on their own line above the property.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — never inline
@Expose() id!: string;
@Column({ name: 'email' }) email!: string;

// ✅ GOOD — decorator above property
@Expose()
id!: string;

@Column({ name: 'email', type: 'varchar', length: 120 })
email!: string;
```

Applies to all property decorators: `@Expose`, `@Column`, `@IsString`, `@IsOptional`, `@Transform`, `@Type`, `@Index`, `@ManyToOne`, `@OneToMany`, `@JoinColumn`, `@WebSocketServer`, etc.

When editing existing code, convert any inline decorator to the two-line form.
